  "Number": 4,
  "Question": "If \\(a\\) is \\(50\\%\\) larger than \\(c,\\) and \\(b\\) is \\(25\\%\\) larger than \\(c,\\) then \\(a\\) is what percent larger than \\(b?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(20\\%\\)",
    "B": "\\(25\\%\\)",
    "C": "\\(50\\%\\)",
    "D": "\\(100\\%\\)",
    "E": "\\(200\\%\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "The requested percentage compares the increase \\(a-b\\) with \\(b\\), because \\(b\\) is the starting amount in this comparison.\n\nThe given increases mean\n\\[\na=1.50c,\\qquad b=1.25c.\n\\]\nSince \\(a-c=0.50c\\) is a positive increase, \\(c>0\\), so \\(b>0\\) and division by \\(b\\) is valid. The increase from \\(b\\) to \\(a\\) is \\(0.25c\\). Therefore the percentage increase is\n\\[\n\\frac{a-b}{b}\\times100\\%\n=\\frac{0.25c}{1.25c}\\times100\\%\n=20\\%.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(20\\%\\), choice A.",
